2           USING THE BY GROUPFORMAT STATEMENT TO PROCESS DATA
                                                           The SAS System

3               This program creates a format that can be used to group data. It shows the use of the groupformat option in the data
3        !  step.
4               Keywords: PROC FORMAT, FORMAT, VALUE, GROUPFORMAT
5               SAS Versions: SAS 9, SAS Viya
6               Documentation:
6        ! https://documentation.sas.com/?cdcId=pgmsascdc&cdcVersion=default&docsetId=proc&docsetTarget=p1xidhqypi0fnwn1if8opjpqpbmn
6        ! .htm
7               1. Create a data set on which to test the new format. The data is sorted by the value to be formatted.
8               2. Use PROC FORMAT with a value statement. Provide ranges for which you want to assign different grouping levels.
9               3. Use the groupformat option on the by statement to allow the data step to read the data by groups.
10              4. Because the data is being read with a by statement the first. and last. variables are created. In this example,
10       ! the
11                 first.salary will be the lowest salary observation for a group and the last.salary observation will be the
11       ! highest.
12              5. In the PROC REPORT apply the format to see the results.
13         ************************************************************************************************/
14         data payroll; /*1*/
15            infile cards;
16            input EmployeeID Salary BirthDate : date9. HireDate : date9.;
17            cards;

NOTE: The data set WORK.PAYROLL has 45 observations and 4 variables.
